ESP32-V3 host with a TI CC2652P (ETH-52P) or CC2652P7 (ETH-52P7) Zigbee radio, IP101 Ethernet PHY, Wi-Fi and USB-C. Both variants share the ESP32 pinout.

The device ships with Inswift's own firmware. Tasmota is an optional alternative for the ESP32: it bridges the CC2652 UART to TCP so ZHA or Zigbee2MQTT can use the gateway over the network. Zigbee2Tasmota, Zigbee Rst 2 and flashing the CC2652 from Tasmota have not been tested on this device.

## Flashing

Flash **Tasmota32 Sonoff-ZigbeeBridgePro** (`tasmota32-zbbrdgpro`) over USB-C with the [Tasmota web installer](https://tasmota.github.io/install/) or esptool. This build includes Ethernet and the TCP serial bridge.

## Configuration

Apply the template, then run:

```console
Backlog TCPBaudRate 115200; TCPConfig 8N1; Rule1 ON System#Boot DO TCPStart 6638 ENDON; Rule1 1; Restart 1
```

If Ethernet does not come up after applying the template:

```console
Backlog EthType 1; EthAddress 1; EthClockMode 0; Ethernet 1
```

Port 6638 matches the stock Inswift firmware. The CC2652 runs Z-Stack coordinator firmware at 115200 baud, no flow control.

**GPIO12 (BSL) must be Output Hi.** The CC2652 bootloader pin idles high, which is the opposite of the Inswift ETH-MG, so do not reuse the ETH-MG template on this device.

| GPIO | Function |
|------|----------|
| 0 | Ethernet clock in |
| 2 / 4 / 14 | RGB LED blue / red / green (PWM) |
| 5 | ETH POWER |
| 12 | Output Hi (CC2652 BSL) |
| 13 / 17 | TCP Rx / TCP Tx (CC2652 UART) |
| 15 | Zigbee Rst 1 (CC2652 nRESET) |
| 18 / 23 | ETH MDIO / ETH MDC |
| 34 | Button_n 1 |

## Home Assistant

- Zigbee2MQTT: `port: tcp://GATEWAY_IP:6638`, `adapter: zstack`, `baudrate: 115200`
- ZHA: radio type ZNP, serial device path `socket://GATEWAY_IP:6638`

